{"title":"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math.</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Logan is constructing a scaled model of his town. The city's water tower stands 40 meters high, and the top portion is a sphere that holds 100,000 liters of water. Logan's miniature water tower holds 0.1 liters. How tall, in meters, should Logan make his tower?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9746a5fddaf3faad195eddcb7c4fb15eccf662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0.04 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{0.4}{\\pi} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 0.4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{4}{\\pi} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"410\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The water tower holds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/8/b78d17d5cd2bc68335bc5ca23bc9c54911fa92e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100,000}{0.1} = 1,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"38\" /> times more water than Logan's miniature. The volume of a sphere is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c214dc015dce30ea587d263eb5899e6f55491760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=\\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />. Since we are comparing the heights (m), we should compare the radii (m) to find the ratio. Since, the radius is cubed, Logan should make his tower <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2d15a7afb6646aada1aee821fadf113762b0909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{1,000,000} = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"152\" height=\"24\" /> times shorter than the actual tower. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67154ae7586c53871ca9362f272ec627691da968.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{100} = \\boxed{0.4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> meters high, or choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Note: The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2d1cb18ffe630676fecf8bce47a5a76d3ebf4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\text{ L}=1,000\\text{ cm}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> doesn't matter since only the ratios are important.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math.\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math.</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by the Beauty of Math.\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube/kU70k1-ONgM?t=154\">https://youtube/kU70k1-ONgM?t=154</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A\">2010 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010